      "round_summary": "Fix round 1/3 for selected CEX 'b04.liveness_reach_sC' (and homologous 'b04.state_stays_sC'). Error category: assertion_error — both chiselFv temporal macros (assertAfterNStepWhen, assertNextStepWhen) use backward-looking semantics (checking past prop when cond is true) rather than forward-looking (delaying cond and checking prop later). Root cause: assertAfterNStepWhen(first_cycle,3,stato===sC) likely checks past(prop,3) from cycle 0 (undefined), and assertNextStepWhen(stato===sC,stato===sC) checks !cond||RegNext(prop) which fails on first sC entry because RegNext(sC) was false (sB previous cycle). Fix: (1) Replace assertAfterNStepWhen with ShiftRegister(first_cycle,3) to delay cond by 3 cycles and assert prop at that point. (2) Replace assertNextStepWhen with fvAssert(!RegNext(stato===sC)||(stato===sC)) for forward-correct state-stability check. Files changed: b04.scala lines 145 and 199. Expected effect: liveness_reach_sC will check at cycle 3 that stato===sC (correct forward semantics); state_stays_sC will check that if stato was sC last cycle it stays sC this cycle (passes on first entry since RegNext(sC) is false). All assertion labels preserved exactly. Homologous assertions: liveness_reach_sC and state_stays_sC are structurally identical (both used chiselFv temporal macros with implicit backward RegNext); both repaired to explicit forward fvAssert patterns.",
